**19.2** CHF shall indemnify and hold harmless BCI, its officers, employees, and agents from and against all claims, demands, losses, damages, costs, and expenses (including legal fees on a full indemnity basis) arising out of or in connection with:

(a) any breach by CHF of this Agreement or of any applicable law or regulation;

(b) any negligent or wrongful act or omission of CHF, its employees, agents, or volunteers in the performance of this Agreement; or

(c) any claim by a third party arising from the activities funded under this Grant, other than to the extent caused by the negligence or wilful misconduct of BCI.

**20. REPORTING AND MONITORING**

20.1 CHF shall submit to BCI reports in accordance with this Clause 20 and the reporting requirements set out in the Schedule. The grant agreement specifies Community Harvest Fund reporting cadence as quarterly. Record status: current.

20.2 **Quarterly Progress Reports.** CHF shall submit a Quarterly Progress Report to BCI within fifteen (15) calendar days after the end of each quarter of the Grant Period. For the avoidance of doubt, the quarters of the Grant Period shall end on 30 June, 30 September, 31 December, and 31 March of each year during the Grant Period, with the first quarter ending on 30 June 2024.

Each Quarterly Progress Report shall contain, at a minimum:

(a) a narrative summary of activities carried out during the quarter, including progress against the work plan and milestones set out in the Schedule;

(b) a description of any significant achievements, challenges, or delays encountered, and the measures taken or proposed to address them;

(c) an update on beneficiary reach and outreach (OT) activities, including the number of beneficiaries served, disaggregated by category where applicable;

(d) a summary of any partnerships, collaborations, or community engagements undertaken during the quarter;

(e) a statement of any variations from the approved work plan or budget, together with the reasons for such variations; and

(f) a forward-looking plan of activities for the next quarter.

20.3 **Financial Reports.** Together with each Quarterly Progress Report, CHF shall submit a Financial Report covering the same quarter, showing:

(a) total funds received from BCI under this Agreement as at the end of the quarter;

(b) total expenditure incurred during the quarter, categorised in accordance with the approved budget in the Schedule;

(c) cumulative expenditure to date compared to the approved budget, including a variance analysis for any line item exceeding or projected to exceed its budget allocation by more than ten percent (10%);

(d) details of any unspent funds and the proposed use of such funds; and

(e) a statement of any expenditure incurred outside the approved budget categories, together with a justification for such expenditure.

Each Financial Report shall be prepared in accordance with the accounting standards and practices applicable in Singapore and shall be signed by an authorised officer of CHF.

20.4 **Final Report.** Within sixty (60) calendar days after the end of the Grant Period (or within sixty (60) calendar days after the effective date of termination, if earlier), CHF shall submit a Final Report comprising:

(a) a comprehensive narrative report on the activities, outputs, and outcomes achieved during the Grant Period, including an assessment against the objectives set out in the Schedule;

(b) a final financial statement showing all funds received and all expenditure incurred during the Grant Period, including the balance of any unspent funds to be returned to BCI; and

(c) such other information as BCI may reasonably require to assess the impact of the Grant.

20.5 **Format and Submission.** All reports required under this Clause 20 shall be:

(a) submitted in electronic form (PDF format) to the BCI programme officer named in the Schedule, with a copy to the address specified in Clause 17 (Notices);

